 "evidence": "Read from two climate-model records written every 13 half-hour steps (6.5 hours). corrected is the corrected design run's year 10 again, from its own year-9 restart, ending on that run's year-10 restart byte for byte: the weather inside one of the design years' own 3-day means, at the level the waters' exchange is paired at and at 10 m over each cell's own ground. earlier is two years of the earlier design case, on today's ground and ten levels, the record the forcing's raise was measured on. One year and two years are short records; the 6.5-hour means are themselves means, and what the wind does inside them is in neither.",
 "reading_rule": "mean_speed_over_vector is the mean speed of the 6.5-hour means over the mean speed of their 3-day mean vectors; cube_ratio is the waters' oxygen study's factor, the cube root of the mean cubed speed over the mean cubed vector speed. excess_rms_m_s is the root of the mean square speed the windows hold beyond their mean vectors. by_vector_speed groups windows of all cells by their mean vector's speed. floored reads the forcing's operation at the lowest level: factor is the mean of the 6.5-hour speeds floored at PlaSim's least wind over the mean of the floored 3-day vector speeds, and quadrature_excess_m_s the excess that, added to the floored vector speed in quadrature, gives a cell's windows their mean speed. Band and surface means weight cells by area; the cells entries are percentiles over cells.",
